        "PMC6006257::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deformation twinning promotes continuous strain hardening and delays plastic localization.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Suppressing deformation twinning will significantly diminish toughness.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard",
        "PMC6006257::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrCoNi is a single-phase FCC alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrCoNi forms deformation-induced nanotwins during mechanical loading.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNi is an example of a metastable FCC high-entropy alloy that naturally forms deformation twins.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adjusting Cr or Al content can alter stacking-fault energy and thereby suppress or enhance twinning.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changing grain size or twin-boundary spacing can suppress or enhance deformation twinning.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The density and distribution of deformation nanotwins govern their effectiveness as barriers to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard",
        "PMC6006257::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deformation twins provide additional obstacles to dislocation glide.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard",
        "PMC6006257::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Obstruction of dislocation glide by twins enhances strain hardening and energy absorption.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "When twinning is suppressed, strain localizes more readily, causing premature failure and reduced fracture toughness.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Samples engineered to enhance twinning will have higher strain-hardening rates than baseline samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard",
        "PMC6006257::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Samples engineered to enhance twinning will have greater ductility and fracture toughness than baseline samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Samples with suppressed twinning will show lower toughness and earlier plastic instability than baseline samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4740901::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
